# 20 — Design gaps
#
# What the fourteen workflows do not yet cover (DIRECTION §6), each to be
# decided as a workflow document and drawn on the canvas before it is built.

task design "Design gaps" {
  depends bootstrap.workflows

  task instruments "Workflow 15: set up an instrument" {
    effort 2d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Tunings, a second instrument, switching, the voicing rules with presets and the expert panel. Explore Chords' DESIGN §2.1, 2.5 are the guide. DIRECTION §6. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/instruments.md"
  }
  task explorer "Workflow 16: the chord explorer" {
    effort 2d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "What 'Explore A on your guitar' opens: fingerings ranked and grouped by position, viewing by notation, starring a shape as my shape. Workflow 2. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/explorer.md"
  }
  task leaving "Workflow 17: leaving" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Deleting an account and taking one's data out; what happens to books others are members of. DIRECTION §6. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/leaving.md"
  }
  task screen_reader "How a screen reader reads a sung line" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "A decided order for chords and words read aloud, and how a chart, a diagram and a conflict are announced. DIRECTION §6. Tests: none — design deliverable (the decided reading order, in a document and on the board); shell.a11y_chart's tests pin it. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/screen_reader.md"
  }
  task theme_picker "Draw the theme picker" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Decided in workflow 1 (automatic: Estante in light mode, Palco in dark); drawn on the account screen. Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow document and its board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/theme_picker.md"
  }
  task home_book_format "The home book's format" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Settings as JSON with a time on every key, so 'the later change wins' key by key; the shelf list, labels, instruments, rules, my shapes, theme, language, variation in use, transpositions. Workflows 8, 13. Tests: none — design deliverable (the format decided in a document); storage.home_book's tests pin it. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/home_book_format.md"
  }
  task example_book "The example book's songs" {
    effort 2d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Songs written for the purpose (no one else's words), voiced for guitar, cavaquinho and ukulele, showing sections, words, variations and a setlist. Ships with the app. Workflow 1. Tests: none in code — each song and the setlist checked canonical with the cifra.md reference before it lands; account.first_run's tests pin them in the app. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/example_book.md"
  }
  task display_preferences "Density and chord-diagram display preferences" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Decide and draw two new user-chosen, synced preferences on the account screen's Preferences section beside theme and language: density (the theme.css densities, today locked at comfortable) and the chord diagram's display — left-handed mirror and vertical/horizontal neck, as Explore Chords offered — applied in the explorer and the in-song picker. Add the home-book registers to docs/home-book-format.md §4.1 and the decision to workflow 1 (density) and workflow 16 (diagram). Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (Density; Left-handed / horizontal-neck). Tests: none — design deliverable (the workflow and home-book-format edits and the Theme-picker board updated). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/display_preferences.md"
  }
  task recovery_email "Setting a recovery email; deleting a passkey-only account" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Decide and draw where a signed-in person sets, verifies (by an emailed link) and changes the recovery email that service.email_links mails — nothing writes accounts.email today, so a passkey-only account has no recovery path. And how a passkey-only account (no email) confirms deletion: a passkey re-authentication in place of the typed email (workflow 17). Workflows 13, 17. Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (Where accounts.email is first written; Passkey-only account cannot confirm deletion). Tests: none — design deliverable (workflow 13 and 17 edits and the boards). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/recovery_email.md"
  }
  task leave_book "Leaving one shared book" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Decide and draw a Leave this book verb for a member who wants to drop one membership without deleting their account: where it sits in book management, its confirmation (unsaved changes and unpushed saves counted, as Remove does), and that Mine on Estante no longer offers the book afterwards. An owner cannot leave (handing ownership stays workflow 10 Later). Workflow 10. Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (Leave one shared book). Tests: none — design deliverable (workflow 10 edit and the board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/leave_book.md"
  }
  task w07_remove_board "Draw the Remove loss-warning cases on W07" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "docs/mockups/W07-add-a-book.dc.html draws only the hosted-in-step Remove one-liner; add the two normative confirmations of workflow 7 L128-135 — unsaved/unpushed loss warning, and the device-only 'gone for good, download first' case — as already implemented by books.online. Publishing the canvas stays a human step (tasks/parking-lot.md, Republish the mockup canvas). Source: tasks/parking-lot.md 2026-10-14 (W07 board under-illustrates the Remove flow). Tests: none — design deliverable (the board). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/w07_remove_board.md"
  }
  task boards_refresh "Redraw the boards where the app follows the workflows" {
    effort 1d
    allocate team
    complete 100
    note "Boards the UI audit found behind their workflows: W01 invited screen (names no book or role before sign-in, workflow 1 L49-56); W03 save sheet (no File name row, workflow 3 Its file name); W05 the unnamed variation is Default; W09 Keep both on a bar conflict and beside Settle in the book panel (workflow 9 Settling one); the tablet song view keeps the search rail beside the song (decided 2026-10-14: the split stays) on W01, W02 and W12; Theme-picker descriptions identical across its frames. Republishing the canvas stays a human step (tasks/parking-lot.md). Source: UI audit 2026-10-14 (app screens vs rendered boards; e2e/web/lib/mockup.js). Tests: none — design deliverable (the boards; audit/render-mockups.mjs renders them). Also (pairwise audit): the explorer on a tablet keeps the search rail; the source editor shows line numbers. Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/boards_refresh.md"
  }
  task sign_in_two_doors "Sign in and make an account as two doors" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    note "Decided 2026-10-19 (launch smoke test): the sign-in surface has two sections, every entry opening the same surface — Already have an account? (use a passkey, or email me a link) and New here? (make an account, which creates a passkey). Today making an account is reachable only from the cold first run, whose row is labelled Sign in but creates (AppShell.jsx:992, FirstRun.jsx:151, SignIn.jsx:175), and from an invitation; the Account screen and Mine on Estante open sign-in only (AppShell.jsx:800, :293), so anyone who used the app locally before signing up has no way to make an account and the browser says there is no passkey for this site. And a signed-out create always makes a new account (service passkeys.go:168-198), so a person with an account who taps the cold row's Sign in on a new device silently gets a second one: the New here? section must say it makes a new account and point an existing one to the other section. Making an account then asks for the recovery email straight away — the same set-and-verify as the account screen's region (workflow 13 §The recovery email), so a new account is not left with no way back if its only passkey is lost; this reverses workflow 13's an account starts with no email and the first run asks for nothing. It can be left for later (Not now), which leaves it to the account screen — It stays skippable (decided 2026-10-19), but while a signed-in account has no confirmed recovery email a fixed banner in the shell says that without one, losing its passkeys loses the account and what is only online — not dismissible, shown on every screen until the address is confirmed (a pending, unconfirmed address keeps it), opening the account screen's recovery-email region. Decide its words (strong and exact about what is lost: the account, its books on Estante, its memberships; not what is on this device), where it sits beside the header chrome and the update-ready notice, and how it reads in Palco and to a screen reader. The Account screen's not-signed-in card draws its own Use a passkey / Email me a link pair (AccountScreen.jsx:659-670) in front of the same surface, and the shell drops which one was pressed (AppShell.jsx:800 opens the method step either way): decide whether the card mirrors the two sections or becomes one entry into them. Decide the copy, the first-run row's name (no longer Sign in alone), where the invited screen's two buttons land, and draw it. Workflows 1 (Cold, Invited), 13 (Signing in, The recovery email). Tests: none — design deliverable (workflow 1 and 13 edits and the W13 and W01 boards, the banner drawn on a phone, tablet and computer). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/sign_in_two_doors.md"
  }
  task book_row_songs "A book on the shelf opens on its songs" {
    effort 0.5d
    allocate team
    note "Decided 2026-10-19 (launch smoke test): pressing a book in the book-management screen opens its songs — search scoped to that book, the address workflow 7 already gives it (…/b/<book>, L52-54) — not its management detail; today the row opens the detail and its one visible button is Files (app/src/books/BooksScreen.jsx:195-219), so the plain way into a book's songs is missing from where books are listed and the advanced one is the default. The row carries one action: managing the book (where it lives, put online, share, download, make it my own, remove — BookDetail) is reached from the book once open, an entry to its detail on the book's songs view (decided 2026-10-19), and Files moves off the row into that detail: the file view is advanced use (workflow 14 §The view says advanced users find it, others never need to). Decide the detail entry's form, name and place on the book's songs view, what the row shows of its songs (a count?), what a book that needs you (workflow 9) opens on, and how it lays out on a tablet and a computer. Workflows 7 (The book-management screen), 14 (The view: where it is reached), 2 if the scoped search changes. Tests: none — design deliverable (workflow 7 and 14 edits and the W07 and W14 boards). Refinement: tasks/refinements/design/book_row_songs.md"
  }
}
